"text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter Visits Vanessa at Work", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "You Are What You Eat", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modal Verbs for Speculating", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Must = it's very likely<br/>Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br/>May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br/>May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He must be at work.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's very likely he's at work.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I can't reach her. Her phone must be off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's likely her phone is off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They could come over for dinner tomorrow.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Coming for dinner tomorrow is possible.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They may not come to the movie tonight. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible they are not coming to the movie tonight.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I guess it might be true. After all, they say \u201cYou are what you eat\u201d.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It could be that you get enough protein from a vegetarian diet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I must be a grilled peanut butter and jelly sandwich! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking for Help and Advice  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are several ways to ask for help in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this. <br/><br/>Let's look at one particular structure for asking for help. This is called a question within a sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the structure:<br/><span class=\"strong\">Can/Could + you + verb</span> (show/tell/explain) + (to) me <span class=\"strong\">+ question word</span> (how...why...where...who...etc.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Can/Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Question Word\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">what</span> are more interesting ideas for meals?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"explain to me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">how</span> a restaurant works?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">how to</span> select meals?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Can you tell me what are more interesting ideas for my meals?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Could you show me how I can select better things to eat?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "poultry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a category of meat that includes birds (chicken, turkey, etc.)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Meat, fish and poultry contain iron, zinc, and B vitamins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about food.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nutrients", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the vitamins and minerals contained in food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Meat and fish are a good source of nutrients.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "burrito", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a dish of meat, vegetables, rice and cheese wrapped in a tortilla", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to be a creamy burrito casserole tomorrow! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "jelly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sweet spread, usually made from fruits", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to be a grilled peanut butter and jelly sandwich! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be a good source of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "containing a lot of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Meat is a good source of protein.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "grains", "type": "name"}, {"content": "food that comes from seeds, like wheat or barley", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The major food groups are grains, vegetables, fruits, milk, meat and beans.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le07ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Ask 6 - 10 people what they had for breakfast and lunch today or yesterday.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the meals for each person on a separate line. Try to include lots of details about each meal, including drinks.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, decide which meal is the most healthy. If you are not sure, go online to find out the nutritional value (protein or nutrients) in different foods.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write the meals in order based on how healthy they are, starting with the most healthy (#1).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present the list to other people in the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk to people about food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss and read about the nutritional value of food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the results.", "type": "text"}]}]}